diff --git a/WYGRAM.md b/WYGRAM.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..5ac1126
--- /dev/null
+++ b/WYGRAM.md
@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+# WyGram 1.0.0
+
+This fork starts from `Swiftgram/Telegram-iOS` commit `cf8b23beaaac4126a396337ac2d5be13f9f76b66`.
+
+## Changes
+
+- Display name, settings labels, watch labels, and localized references use WyGram.
+- The main MTProto session sends `WyGram` as its device model label. Telegram controls the separate app name shown in Devices using the application's registered `api_id`; register that API application as WyGram.
+- Swiftgram's local Pro settings and badges are available to all users. The paywall routes to the features page. StoreKit product requests and the startup subscription check are removed.
+- Requests to Swiftgram's settings service now have timeouts so a resumed app cannot wait indefinitely on those requests.
+- The upstream icon remains in place for this first test version.
+
+Telegram Premium, Stars, paid messages, and anything enforced by Telegram or Swiftgram servers are unchanged. The background loading problem was reported after resuming the app; the startup subscription query had a documented hang risk and has been removed, but device testing and logs are still needed to confirm the full cause.
+
+## Build requirements
+
+Build on macOS with Xcode 26.2 and the Bazel version in `versions.json`. Before building, create an application at [my.telegram.org](https://my.telegram.org/apps) named WyGram and enter its `api_id` and `api_hash` into a private copy of `build-system/template_minimal_development_configuration.json`. Replace the placeholder bundle identifier and Team ID with your own values. Do not commit secrets or signing files.
+
+An installable IPA requires a device signing certificate and provisioning profile. The upstream README documents project generation and the `build` command. Test the resulting build by signing in, opening local features, moving the app to the background, and returning after both short and long delays on Wi-Fi and cellular data.
